1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:55,889
This is so nice.

3
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:57,140
That's right!

4
00:00:57,223 --> 00:00:59,726
Today's your birthday.
Is there anything you want to do?

5
00:01:00,935 --> 00:01:02,187
I never thought about it.

6
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:05,106
Want to go see my family?

7
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:07,650
What?

8
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:09,069
I have family too.

9
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:12,614
A grandmother who accepts me
without any questions.

10
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:14,199
I just asked my family to return.

11
00:01:14,282 --> 00:01:15,867
Do you have a problem with that?

12
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:20,205
<i>Sisters who always have my back.</i>

13
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:22,499
<i>I was your closest friend in the village.</i>

14
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:25,376
A friend with the purest of hearts, and a…

15
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:26,836
Slightly older brother-in-law.

16
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,798
A <i>slightly </i>older brother-in-law.

17
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:33,468
You can ask me to run errands
as much as you want.

18
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:35,762
And a dutiful younger brother.

19
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:39,641
I miss them all so much.

20
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,024
This is nice.

21
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:07,335
I'll have grilled whole potatoes,
sausage, and rice cake skewers.

22
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:08,628
What about you?

23
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:13,049
<i>Oppa</i>, come here.

24
00:02:16,761 --> 00:02:18,096
<i>Oppa</i>, should we get coffee?

25
00:02:18,888 --> 00:02:20,306
I want an iced mocha. You?

26
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:23,852
<i>Oppa</i>, do you have a hole in your chin?

27
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:25,520
This is really good.

28
00:02:26,062 --> 00:02:27,147
<i>Oppa</i>, say "ah."

29
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:30,150
<i>Oppa</i>, you okay?

30
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:34,320
Jang Tae-ha.

31
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:35,572
Yeah?

32
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:37,198
I asked what you're going to eat.

33
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:40,702
Right. I'll have what you're having.

34
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:45,039
Two butter-grilled potatoes,
two sausage and rice cake skewers, please.

35
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:47,417
Here, look at this.

36
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,210
-Goodness, ma'am!
-Why?

37
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:52,422
-Ma'am.
-Did you go grocery shopping?

38
00:02:52,505 --> 00:02:53,673
Yes.

39
00:02:54,465 --> 00:02:56,467
It's Tae-ha's birthday today.

40
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,469
Wait. Is that so?

41
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,387
Yes.

42
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:02,432
That's right. Tae-ha's birthday
was around this time of year.

43
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:04,726
-You're right.
-Today's his birthday.

44
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:08,563
Oh, I see you're all here.
Jeong-hwa is back.

45
00:03:08,646 --> 00:03:10,190
-Careful.
-Jeong…

46
00:03:10,273 --> 00:03:12,275
-Jeong-hwa.
-Hello.

47
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:13,902
-I'm back.
-Jeong-hwa.

48
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:16,029
-Are you feeling better?
-Yes.

49
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:17,614
While I was hospitalized,

50
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:20,742
we got to spend time glued to each other,
like newlyweds again.

51
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:24,078
Thank goodness
the car accident wasn't worse.

52
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:25,371
-Exactly.
-Yes.

53
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:29,083
It's Tae-ha's birthday today,
so we hurried over here.

54
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:31,961
Ma'am, I'll help you with the food later.

55
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:34,923
-Goodness, no.
-You don't need to help.

56
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:36,049
We'll help out.

57
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:38,343
-I'm fine.
-You should rest.

58
00:03:39,093 --> 00:03:41,095
I'll help out too!

59
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:45,475
Eun-sae!

60
00:03:46,851 --> 00:03:48,645
-Grandma!
-Oh, yes. Goodness me.

61
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:51,356
Good heavens, what's happening?

62
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:53,316
Goodness, you're here.

63
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,109
Ms. Prosecutor.

64
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:59,781
I thought I was Tae-ha's wife here,
not a prosecutor.

65
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:01,282
What's going on?

66
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:04,369
I thought you'd never come here again.

67
00:04:04,452 --> 00:04:06,287
That's impossible.

68
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:09,624
Because our connection…

69
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:15,213
is like taffy.

70
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:17,674
That's right.

71
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:19,968
Welcome back.

72
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:22,136
-Ladies.
-Welcome back.

73
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:27,600
-I missed you.
-Me too.

74
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:30,520
Well done for coming back.

75
00:04:30,603 --> 00:04:32,272
We only got to see you on TV.

76
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:35,358
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

77
00:04:35,441 --> 00:04:38,361
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

78
00:04:38,444 --> 00:04:41,823
<i>Happy birthday dear Jang Tae-ha</i>

79
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:44,701
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

80
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:48,538
-Make a wish.
-Go on.

81
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,791
We can hear you.

82
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:53,001
He's like a kid.

83
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:00,383
-Happy birthday!
-Happy birthday.

84
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:01,301
Happy birthday.

85
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,385
Happy birthday.

86
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:04,387
Thank you all so much.

87
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:07,056
Tae-ha, is there anything you want?

88
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,599
It'll be our treat.

89
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:10,476
Come on, Hui-ja.

90
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,186
What could we possibly give him

91
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,772
that would compare to the gift
he already received?

92
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:15,815
That's true.

93
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:19,068
His fake bride has become his real bride.

94
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:21,070
What gift could possibly top that?

95
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:23,239
Oh, come on.

96
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:26,617
You two sure took the long way around.

97
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:31,497
Now all that's left is for them to live
happily ever after like us.

98
00:05:36,878 --> 00:05:38,129
Now that I think about it,

99
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:40,048
they're the spitting image.

100
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:41,507
Sorry?

101
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:42,592
Who is?

102
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:46,512
Her and Tae-ha's mom.

103
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:47,847
Sorry?

104
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:50,183
Me and Tae-ha's mother?

105
00:05:57,774 --> 00:06:00,943
32 YEARS AGO

106
00:06:04,238 --> 00:06:05,114
Are your feet cold?

107
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:08,993
How pretty.

108
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:14,791
<i>Along the fruit farm path</i>
<i>Outside the village</i>

109
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:19,295
<i>The African flowers are in full bloom</i>

110
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:22,465
Isn't it "acacia"?

111
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:23,883
Pardon?

112
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:28,763
Acacia.

113
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:33,101
Acacia.

114
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:42,318
You look like you're from out of town,
not from Gujin.

115
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:43,736
That's right.

116
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:47,323
I came after hearing about a dishwashing
job that came with room and board,

117
00:06:47,407 --> 00:06:49,117
but they already hired someone.

118
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:52,328
How old?

119
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:54,455
Six months.

120
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:56,165
No, I meant…

121
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:19,981
There's a sink full of dishes
back at my place too.

122
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:25,486
I guess you could stay with me tonight
if you have nowhere else to go.

123
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:41,878
What are you doing?

124
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:45,256
Don't stand around.
Lay him in there and get him comfy.

125
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:49,886
Thank you.

126
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:08,779
The sunset is so pretty from here!

127
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:12,450
It's so spectacle.

128
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:14,744
"Spectacular."

129
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,837
I was planning on going to night school
once the baby's a bit older.

130
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:30,635
You don't look that old yourself, lady.

131
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:32,595
I'm 23.

132
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:35,056
So I'm technically a young lady.

133
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:38,267
I guess so.

134
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:44,398
My daughter would be your age
if she were still alive.

135
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:48,736
And the baby's dad?

136
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:52,615
He's not around.
I'm raising him on my own.

137
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:54,742
No parents to rely on?

138
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:56,494
None.

139
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:58,829
That's why I'm four in one.

140
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:03,167
His grandma, grandpa, and dad.
I'll be everything for him.

141
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:08,130
A baby doesn't need a smart mom
who went to college.

142
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:11,175
The best mom is one
who showers her baby with love.

143
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:20,393
I'll cook dinner today to repay you
for letting us stay the night.

144
00:09:20,476 --> 00:09:23,020
Well, if you say so.

145
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:32,697
Please try it.

146
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,913
Golly, you make a mean gochujang stew.

147
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,540
Where did you learn to make this?

148
00:09:43,332 --> 00:09:45,626
I've just made it a lot.

149
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:47,378
Because someone likes it.

150
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:55,136
Didn't you say you're four in one?

151
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:59,432
You should eat four times as much
so you have the energy to raise your baby.

152
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:05,229
No one really knows
how my Tae-ha's life will turn out.

153
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:07,815
Just look at <i>The Last Match</i>.

154
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:09,859
It looks like
Son Ji-chang's team will win,

155
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:12,903
but in the end,
Jang Dong-gun makes a dunk,

156
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,488
and his team wins.

157
00:10:15,072 --> 00:10:17,241
Life is like a basketball game.

158
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:20,286
My Tae-ha may not have the best luck
when it comes to parents,

159
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:23,372
but who knows if he'll throw down
a huge dunk later in life?

160
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,626
Who says he's unlucky?

161
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:29,670
Look at those chubby cheeks of his.

162
00:10:29,754 --> 00:10:32,506
They're so chubby,
they might burst any minute.

163
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:37,261
You're like a skewer,
and yet you've fed him so well.

164
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:39,639
You can search all over the country.

165
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,807
There aren't many mothers
as admirable as you.

166
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:46,854
I'm admirable?

167
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:47,813
Of course.

168
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:51,359
With no one to rely on, you still
protected your child with all your might.

169
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:53,653
If you're not an admirable mother, who is?

170
00:10:57,531 --> 00:10:58,866
If you have nowhere to go,

171
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:01,911
do you want to just stay here
and make taffy with me?

172
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:06,874
Really?

173
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:10,336
I'll even throw your baby
a great first birthday party.

174
00:11:15,549 --> 00:11:16,634
Hurry and eat up.

175
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:23,307
Goodness, I doubt
you're even eating regular meals.

176
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:24,809
Here, have some hairtail.

177
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:26,894
HAPPY FIRST BIRTHDAY

178
00:11:26,977 --> 00:11:30,439
The baby is the star of the show.
Why would I dress up?

179
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:31,899
Please hold still.

180
00:11:31,982 --> 00:11:35,611
A first birthday photo is forever.
His grandma should be pretty.

181
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:37,947
There.

182
00:11:38,447 --> 00:11:40,324
-That's enough.
-All done.

183
00:11:41,325 --> 00:11:42,284
All right.

184
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:43,703
Okay.

185
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:46,080
Let's see what our Tae-ha will pick.

186
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:47,540
-All right.
-What's your pick?

187
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:51,168
Okay, Tae-ha.
Which one of these takes your fancy?

188
00:11:51,252 --> 00:11:52,545
Let's grab one.

189
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:54,255
Good boy. The gavel.

190
00:11:54,338 --> 00:11:56,090
Grab the gavel. Go on.

191
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:57,633
That's it. Good boy.

192
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:05,182
<i>She lived a lonely life without any</i>
<i>belongings in the world to call her own,</i>

193
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:07,935
<i>and yet she never lost heart</i>
<i>and stayed so bright.</i>

194
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:15,443
And just like a certain someone,
she hated being called "lady."

195
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:20,823
Seeing you with such a good person
and being so affectionate with her…

196
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,951
I'm sure Tae-ha's mom is smiling

197
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:25,786
way up there.

198
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:27,538
Yes.

199
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:30,040
She's probably smiling with happiness.

200
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:33,002
-I'm sure she is.
-Yes.

201
00:12:33,085 --> 00:12:35,713
Tae-ha's mom, thank you for the food!

202
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:37,506
Thank you for the food!

203
00:12:38,632 --> 00:12:40,092
-Let's eat.
-Please eat.

204
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:43,345
Ma'am, when are you going back to Seoul?

205
00:12:48,309 --> 00:12:49,852
I have to leave soon.

206
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:52,146
-You're leaving already?
-So soon?

207
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:54,732
It's not even taffy-making day today,

208
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:58,652
but I guess the whole village
will smell sickly sweet later.

209
00:12:58,736 --> 00:13:00,654
Oh my goodness!

210
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,950
I told you I'd drive you to Seoul.

211
00:13:05,534 --> 00:13:07,661
I told you I don't want to hassle you.

212
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:09,705
I told you, I'm fine.

213
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:12,082
And I told you, I'm really fine.

214
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:25,846
Just look at them.

215
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:29,850
I'm going to miss you so much
until the weekend.

216
00:13:32,436 --> 00:13:33,354
Me too.

217
00:13:37,525 --> 00:13:38,359
Hold up.

218
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:43,280
You said I was the one and only woman
in your life.

219
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:45,699
Does that mean
this is your first real relationship?

220
00:13:45,783 --> 00:13:49,161
-Yes, he's been single since birth.
-It's his first.

221
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:53,499
So what if it's my first?

222
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:58,337
Speaking from experience,

223
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,923
starting tomorrow, people will look at you

224
00:14:01,006 --> 00:14:02,716
like you're a lunatic.

225
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:07,054
-Looks delicious.
-It does.

226
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:18,858
-Are you nuts?
-Sorry?

227
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:21,777
Even an Olympic gold medalist
wouldn't smile as wide as you.

228
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:28,200
So this is what she meant.

229
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:32,621
<i>And suddenly,</i>

230
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:35,541
<i>everything in the world</i>
<i>will look beautiful.</i>

231
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:37,877
What are you doing? What are you saying?

232
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,253
Hey, Tae-ha!

233
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:41,046
-Hello.
-Hi.

234
00:14:43,007 --> 00:14:44,675
-A bird pooped on him.
-Bird poop?

235
00:14:44,758 --> 00:14:45,968
-Yeah.
-Oh dear.

236
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:49,179
That's what bird poop looks like?

237
00:14:49,763 --> 00:14:50,806
Is he smiling?

238
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:53,559
What, is he that bird expert, Yun Mu-bu?

239
00:14:53,642 --> 00:14:56,729
Why is he looking so lovingly
at bird poop?

240
00:14:58,022 --> 00:15:01,025
Try giving him cow or dog poop.

241
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:05,112
Right now, even a field of poop
will look like a field of flowers to him.

242
00:15:06,196 --> 00:15:07,823
-Look at this.
-Look at what?

243
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,408
What bird do you think did this?

244
00:15:09,491 --> 00:15:11,035
-Stay away!
-What the heck?

245
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:15,539
<i>And you'll feel a new sense of gratitude</i>
<i>for the invention of cell phones.</i>

246
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:19,668
<i>I feel like I can finally breathe,</i>
<i>seeing your face like this.</i>

247
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:22,630
How did people
from the Goryeo and Joseon periods

248
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:24,632
endure their lovesickness without phones?

249
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:26,383
Maybe that's why they died so young.

250
00:15:29,261 --> 00:15:30,679
<i>We'll finally meet up tomorrow.</i>

251
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:35,351
Yeah. I'm going to stick to you like glue
all day tomorrow.

252
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,520
<i>By the way, what should we</i>

253
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:39,813
call each other?

254
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:41,523
-Call each other?
<i>-Yes.</i>

255
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:44,234
<i>It feels a bit too formal</i>
<i>always calling you "Jang Tae-ha."</i>

256
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,321
Oppa<i>.</i>

257
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:50,658
<i>Oppa</i>, do you have a hole in your chin?

258
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:51,742
<i>Oppa</i>, say "ah."

259
00:15:51,825 --> 00:15:52,701
<i>Oppa</i>, you okay?

260
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:58,624
<i>"</i>Oppa<i>"</i>

261
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,085
<i>is a bit too cliché.</i>

262
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:06,090
Right. I think so too.

263
00:16:07,299 --> 00:16:08,509
<i>What else is there?</i>

264
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:11,095
Just call me anything.

265
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:12,972
<i>I don't care what we call each other.</i>

266
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:15,349
Really?

267
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:17,476
Well, okay.

268
00:16:17,559 --> 00:16:19,061
I'll pick you up tomorrow.

269
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:20,813
Okay.

270
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:25,067
I'll look so good tomorrow
that I'll blow you away. Just you wait.

271
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:59,435
Jang Tae-ha.

272
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,230
I missed you.

273
00:17:03,814 --> 00:17:04,648
Me too.

274
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:08,944
Let's have lots of fun this weekend.

275
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:11,572
I worked all night yesterday to do that.

276
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:16,201
I think you're still working hard.

277
00:17:19,329 --> 00:17:20,164
You mean my looks?

278
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:21,999
Yeah.

279
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:24,126
Let's hurry and go.

280
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:31,050
I'll choose the music.

281
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:32,384
Sure.

282
00:17:33,635 --> 00:17:37,765
It's been a while, so maybe we should
listen to my favorite g.o.d <i>oppas.</i>

283
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:40,642
Your g.o.d <i>oppas</i>?

284
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:41,685
Yes.

285
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:43,520
What's wrong with my g.o.d <i>oppas</i>?

286
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,148
Huh? Nothing.

287
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:47,733
It's good to hear.

288
00:17:53,697 --> 00:17:54,782
"<i>Oppa</i>"…

289
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:58,452
is a bit too cliché.

290
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:02,664
<i>Right. I think so too.</i>

291
00:18:03,957 --> 00:18:07,503
Are we a year apart?

292
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:11,340
Yes, I'm 33, and you're 34.

293
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:12,674
Right.

294
00:18:19,306 --> 00:18:20,849
We're so old, aren't we?

295
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:22,559
Yeah.

296
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:26,688
But I'm a year older than you, huh?

297
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:31,860
That's okay.

298
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:33,695
Stay strong.

299
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:51,713
And thumbs up, please. All right.

300
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:53,715
Take the picture. Smile.

301
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:55,050
That's good.

302
00:18:55,759 --> 00:18:57,761
-Let me see. Did it come out nice?
-Yeah.

303
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:00,514
It looks good.

304
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:02,057
Why are we taking pictures?

305
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:04,935
I have to brag about my friendship
with the star prosecutor.

306
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:09,356
You could even say that our clinic
produced said star prosecutor.

307
00:19:09,439 --> 00:19:10,274
Right?

308
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:12,818
Yes, well, thank you.

309
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:16,405
I probably got my memory back
thanks to your treatment.

310
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:20,033
As if I'd fall for that.

311
00:19:20,117 --> 00:19:21,743
You remembered.

312
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:23,412
You know,

313
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:27,082
it's great that you remembered
and are going back to your old life,

314
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:30,127
but I'm a little sad
that I won't be able to see you anymore.

315
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:33,463
Sure, we won't be seeing each other
as doctor and patient,

316
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:35,966
but our relationship is still precious.

317
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:39,303
Going forward, I'll consider you my <i>oppa</i>.

318
00:19:39,845 --> 00:19:40,971
What?

319
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:43,974
Why are you shocked?

320
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:48,187
Then should we cut ties
because I'm done with treatment?

321
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,147
Yeah, she can consider me her <i>oppa</i>.

322
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:51,648
Bring it in.

323
00:19:57,821 --> 00:19:59,031
Eun-sae.

324
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:00,782
Gi-jun <i>oppa</i>?

325
00:20:03,785 --> 00:20:05,245
Hey, that's not bad.

326
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,166
Yeah, that's better.

327
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:15,797
Isn't it so nice to be back here
after so long?

328
00:20:19,509 --> 00:20:21,595
What's wrong, Jang Tae-ha?

329
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:25,015
Gi-jun and I

330
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:26,808
are the same age.

331
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:30,020
I know.
You two were high school classmates.

332
00:20:31,438 --> 00:20:34,024
Yeah, we were classmates.

333
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:39,321
I'll get the car.

334
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:45,244
So cute.

335
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,704
How is he so adorable?

336
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:52,209
Yesterday, he was all,
"I don't care what we call each other."

337
00:20:53,001 --> 00:20:55,003
Jang Tae-ha, let's go together.

338
00:20:59,216 --> 00:21:00,092
This is good.

339
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:04,179
Isn't it hard going back and forth
between Taffy Village and Seoul?

340
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:07,849
It's not hard at all.
All the people I want to see are here.

341
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:11,186
We went to see someone I'd missed today.

342
00:21:11,812 --> 00:21:12,646
Really? Who?

343
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:14,231
Gi-jun <i>oppa</i>.

344
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:20,529
Gi-jun, as in Tae-ha's friend
who treated you?

345
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:21,571
-Yes.
-I see.

346
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:24,992
But since he's not treating me anymore,
he's not my doctor.

347
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:26,368
That makes sense.

348
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:27,661
That's right.

349
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:30,664
If we're just talking about looks,

350
00:21:30,747 --> 00:21:33,333
I look older than you,
so I could be your <i>oppa </i>too.

351
00:21:33,875 --> 00:21:36,336
That's true. You're absolutely right.

352
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:39,214
People who don't know us would think
you're my <i>oppa</i>.

353
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:40,215
That's right.

354
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:42,509
Should I just call you <i>oppa </i>then?

355
00:21:42,592 --> 00:21:44,720
Then should we try hearing it?

356
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:47,222
Gang-rok <i>oppa</i>.

357
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:49,975
I like that.

358
00:21:51,977 --> 00:21:54,438
What? Why are you getting up
in the middle of eating?

359
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:56,690
To feed the dog.

360
00:21:57,899 --> 00:21:58,942
Dogs get hungry too.

361
00:22:00,110 --> 00:22:01,194
Come when you're done.

362
00:22:14,374 --> 00:22:15,334
Stop it.

363
00:22:15,417 --> 00:22:17,044
-Yeah.
-You'll make the kid cry.

364
00:22:17,127 --> 00:22:18,045
Did you notice?

365
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:19,087
Of course we did!

366
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:22,758
If you had gone on any longer,
you would have called me <i>oppa </i>too.

367
00:22:24,634 --> 00:22:28,764
I just love how that <i>oppa</i>
acts like a blushing teen. He's adorable.

368
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:34,394
Go and cheer him up. I bet his insides
are more burnt than this scorched rice.

369
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:37,522
-I'll be right back.
-You don't have to come back.

370
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:40,484
How can he be such a fool?

371
00:22:40,567 --> 00:22:41,860
Fool. A total fool.

372
00:22:45,530 --> 00:22:46,698
Jang Tae-ha.

373
00:22:47,824 --> 00:22:49,743
Jang Tae-ha.

374
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:54,247
How could you go home without me?

375
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:00,545
I was worried Blessing might be hungry.

376
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:07,052
Are you sulking right now, Jang Tae-ha?

377
00:23:07,135 --> 00:23:08,845
No! Me?

378
00:23:10,013 --> 00:23:13,225
Even someone riding the bullet train
could see you're sulking.

379
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:14,768
I'm not though.

380
00:23:14,851 --> 00:23:16,019
You are though.

381
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,188
Do you think I don't know you?

382
00:23:18,271 --> 00:23:20,399
I can tell just by your face, Jang Tae-ha.

383
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:25,195
The whole "Jang Tae-ha" thing…

384
00:23:25,862 --> 00:23:27,155
Gi-jun is an <i>oppa.</i>

385
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:30,325
Gang-rok is an <i>oppa. </i>Even g.o.d are <i>oppas</i>.
So why am I the only one…

386
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:36,164
Well, forget it.

387
00:23:40,377 --> 00:23:43,130
You're really leaving me behind, babe?

388
00:23:49,010 --> 00:23:51,054
I'm asking if you're going alone.

389
00:23:51,138 --> 00:23:52,973
Babe.

390
00:24:06,736 --> 00:24:10,824
I can call anyone "<i>oppa</i>."
"Babe" is so much better.

391
00:24:11,324 --> 00:24:12,617
Don't you think, babe?

392
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:17,080
Yeah.

393
00:24:20,083 --> 00:24:22,419
Did you want me to call you "<i>oppa</i>"
that badly?

394
00:24:22,502 --> 00:24:23,587
Tae-ha <i>oppa</i>.

395
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:25,964
<i>Oppa.</i>

396
00:24:26,047 --> 00:24:27,132
Oh, stop it.

397
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:28,633
Should I?

398
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:32,304
Then should I call you Jang Tae-ha again?
And speak to you politely?

399
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:38,560
Come on, <i>oppa</i>! Tae-ha <i>oppa</i>.

400
00:24:39,060 --> 00:24:41,938
<i>Oppa</i>.

401
00:24:42,022 --> 00:24:42,939
Babe.

402
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:45,609
Babe.

403
00:24:45,692 --> 00:24:46,776
Seriously.

404
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:48,195
Oh, come on.

405
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:50,238
I mean, I like it, but…

406
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:51,364
But?

407
00:24:53,950 --> 00:24:55,785
It really is home sweet home.

408
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:00,957
But

409
00:25:02,375 --> 00:25:04,586
what should I call you?

410
00:25:06,254 --> 00:25:09,508
Do I keep calling you "Go Eun-sae"?

411
00:25:09,591 --> 00:25:12,844
What's wrong with that?
I like hearing that name so much.

412
00:25:13,970 --> 00:25:16,556
-Because your mother gave you that name?
-Yes, exactly.

413
00:25:18,391 --> 00:25:19,809
This is just my guess,

414
00:25:20,393 --> 00:25:25,398
but I think my mom dreamt of a pretty bird
when she was pregnant with me.

415
00:25:25,899 --> 00:25:26,775
That could be true.

416
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:27,859
Right?

417
00:25:31,988 --> 00:25:35,575
I wonder why your mother
named you "Tae-ha."

418
00:25:37,577 --> 00:25:38,537
I don't know.

419
00:25:40,372 --> 00:25:42,958
Maybe she wanted me to become
a strong person

420
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:46,253
who can embrace everything
like a big river.

421
00:25:52,926 --> 00:25:55,887
But embracing everything and being patient

422
00:25:56,429 --> 00:25:57,806
is really hard to do.

423
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:04,104
I don't think she wanted her child
to just be strong.

424
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:14,656
I want to ask her, but I can't.

425
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:19,703
Where is your mother?

426
00:26:21,705 --> 00:26:24,332
She's in a place
overlooking the entire village.

427
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:29,045
Let's go see her together sometime.

428
00:26:31,673 --> 00:26:32,674
Okay.

429
00:26:35,427 --> 00:26:38,138
Time goes by too fast when we're together.

430
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:40,932
I have to go back to Seoul tomorrow.

431
00:26:42,934 --> 00:26:45,854
-You have so much work, right?
-Yeah, until the trial.

432
00:26:47,814 --> 00:26:49,899
Is there anything I can help you with?

433
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:54,738
There is.

434
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:58,241
Do you know what Baek Sang-gil
used to do a long time ago?

435
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:01,202
-A long time ago?
-It was a long time ago.

436
00:27:01,786 --> 00:27:04,539
I found something suspicious
in his office.

437
00:27:09,628 --> 00:27:10,462
SEOUL BIRTH REGISTER

438
00:27:10,545 --> 00:27:14,049
We found this in your safe
while searching your office.

439
00:27:15,592 --> 00:27:20,555
It appears to be a register of births
in Seoul from May 1993 to 1994.

440
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:21,848
You remember it, right?

441
00:27:23,099 --> 00:27:25,477
I grew up in an orphanage,
so I know how it goes.

442
00:27:26,061 --> 00:27:28,855
The illegal adoption of infants
and trafficking of newborns.

443
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:31,316
Were you involved
in that sort of thing back then?

444
00:27:32,317 --> 00:27:35,028
I'm going to ask for life imprisonment
for you anyway.

445
00:27:35,654 --> 00:27:38,365
Adding one more crime
won't change your sentence,

446
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:39,616
so why not just admit it?

447
00:27:39,699 --> 00:27:42,452
Adding one less crime
won't change my sentence either,

448
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:46,039
so why not just stop digging?

449
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:08,228
REHABILITATION

450
00:28:12,649 --> 00:28:17,362
<i>It appears to be a register of births</i>
<i>in Seoul from May 1993 to 1994.</i>

451
00:28:17,862 --> 00:28:18,988
<i>You remember it, right?</i>

452
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:37,841
You're smoking a lot today.

453
00:28:38,383 --> 00:28:39,968
Do you have a lot on your mind?

454
00:28:44,097 --> 00:28:44,931
I guess so.

455
00:28:46,266 --> 00:28:47,976
They keep making me think about

456
00:28:49,561 --> 00:28:51,146
useless memories.

457
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:54,649
It's all because of one guy.

458
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:59,279
All of this happened
because he disobeyed me.

459
00:29:00,530 --> 00:29:03,074
Even the memories
that I didn't have to remember.

460
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:08,037
I should've nipped that trouble
in the bud long ago.

461
00:29:16,296 --> 00:29:18,089
It's time to cut it down.

462
00:29:21,801 --> 00:29:24,137
<i>The first trial</i>
<i>of former Gangju Mayor Ju Min-jong</i>

463
00:29:24,220 --> 00:29:26,431
<i>and Chairman Baek of Mirae Eden</i>
<i>will be held</i>

464
00:29:26,514 --> 00:29:28,850
<i>at the Seoul Eastern District Court</i>
<i>this morning.</i>

465
00:29:28,933 --> 00:29:31,561
<i>The prosecution is being led</i>
<i>by Prosecutor Go Ji-won.</i>

466
00:29:32,896 --> 00:29:36,858
Furthermore, considering the antisocial
charges that have been uncovered,

467
00:29:36,941 --> 00:29:39,027
we seek 15 years' imprisonment
for Ju Min-jong

468
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:42,947
and life imprisonment for Baek Sang-gil.

469
00:29:47,702 --> 00:29:49,078
Here, just a moment!

470
00:29:57,295 --> 00:29:59,172
Please say a few words!

471
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:11,226
THE LATE JANG HYE-SU

472
00:30:12,352 --> 00:30:13,228
Mom.

473
00:30:14,771 --> 00:30:16,564
You've been watching everything, right?

474
00:30:18,024 --> 00:30:21,236
I'm sorry for disappointing you until now.

475
00:30:23,279 --> 00:30:24,280
But…

476
00:30:26,658 --> 00:30:28,243
I like how things are now.

477
00:30:30,954 --> 00:30:32,372
Now I'm truly…

478
00:30:35,458 --> 00:30:36,543
happy.

479
00:31:01,734 --> 00:31:04,153
You did a great job
getting through a big case.

480
00:31:05,029 --> 00:31:08,700
It's a shame because it seems like
there are still more crimes to uncover.

481
00:31:09,534 --> 00:31:12,704
They're such old cases
that many of them lack any evidence.

482
00:31:13,955 --> 00:31:14,831
Let's take it slow.

483
00:31:14,914 --> 00:31:15,915
Prosecutor!

484
00:31:18,209 --> 00:31:20,336
Baek Sang-gil escaped
the prison transport van.

485
00:31:21,504 --> 00:31:22,714
What the hell do you mean?

486
00:31:31,306 --> 00:31:32,974
EUN-SAE, HONG DO-YEOP, KIM GANG-ROK

487
00:31:37,729 --> 00:31:38,855
Sir!

488
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:43,151
-Hurry up.
-What's going on?

489
00:31:43,651 --> 00:31:45,570
-How come you're…
-Baek Sang-gil escaped.

490
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:50,700
Yeah.

491
00:31:51,367 --> 00:31:52,285
You're okay, right?

492
00:31:52,368 --> 00:31:53,494
Yeah, I'm okay.

493
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:57,081
I'm under government protection,
and Violent Crimes is heading to Gujin.

494
00:31:57,707 --> 00:31:58,541
Here?

495
00:31:58,625 --> 00:32:01,419
<i>If he escaped to hide or to stow away,</i>
<i>that'd be some relief.</i>

496
00:32:01,502 --> 00:32:04,839
But if he escaped to get revenge,
then Taffy Village could be a target.

497
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:06,883
Just be careful until then.

498
00:32:06,966 --> 00:32:09,177
I'll join you as soon as things
are settled here.

499
00:32:11,512 --> 00:32:14,933
Nothing suggests
that Baek Sang-gil is headed here.

500
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:17,769
We're just preparing
for the worst-case scenario.

501
00:32:18,269 --> 00:32:19,354
Don't get scared yet.

502
00:32:20,396 --> 00:32:21,356
Okay.

503
00:32:26,319 --> 00:32:27,153
And Grandma?

504
00:32:39,874 --> 00:32:41,834
What's all that noise?

505
00:32:43,002 --> 00:32:43,836
Okay.

506
00:33:51,988 --> 00:33:54,574
-What about Jang Tae-ha?
-The boys are looking for him.

507
00:34:08,463 --> 00:34:10,381
What is it? Is she not picking up?

508
00:34:10,882 --> 00:34:13,468
No. I can't reach Song-wol either.

509
00:34:14,010 --> 00:34:15,470
GRANDMA

510
00:34:16,512 --> 00:34:17,346
Grandma.

511
00:34:17,430 --> 00:34:18,264
<i>It's been a while.</i>

512
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:23,352
If you bring the police and make a fuss,
the old woman dies.

513
00:34:26,981 --> 00:34:28,024
Come alone.

514
00:34:28,524 --> 00:34:30,735
No. Don't come! You can't come here!

515
00:34:30,818 --> 00:34:32,195
-Grandma, you okay?
<i>-Tae-ha!</i>

516
00:34:32,278 --> 00:34:33,446
Don't you dare come--

517
00:34:33,529 --> 00:34:34,739
Grandma!

518
00:34:34,822 --> 00:34:36,240
Grandma, can you hear me?

519
00:34:37,950 --> 00:34:40,411
Baek Sang-gil, you bastard.

520
00:34:46,292 --> 00:34:47,293
Sir.

521
00:34:49,212 --> 00:34:50,880
-Let's go around.
-There's no time.

522
00:34:53,132 --> 00:34:54,926
-You can't.
-Coach.

523
00:34:55,009 --> 00:34:56,094
Not alone.

524
00:34:56,886 --> 00:34:58,846
We need at least three for that many.

525
00:35:04,769 --> 00:35:06,813
Everyone, please don't get hurt.

526
00:35:34,841 --> 00:35:36,175
Jang Tae-ha!

527
00:35:42,431 --> 00:35:43,516
Fuck!

528
00:35:56,571 --> 00:35:57,446
Damn it!

529
00:35:57,947 --> 00:35:59,824
Man, this isn't easy.

530
00:36:53,169 --> 00:36:54,378
When she was alive,

531
00:36:54,462 --> 00:36:58,090
she was a mother
who would protect her child with her life.

532
00:36:59,550 --> 00:37:02,470
I'm sure she's protecting her child
from heaven too.

533
00:37:03,387 --> 00:37:05,806
You won't be able to touch Tae-ha.

534
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:08,851
You won't touch him. Never!

535
00:37:20,529 --> 00:37:21,864
There's something

536
00:37:23,449 --> 00:37:25,493
<i>in this world</i>
<i>that you can never win against.</i>

537
00:38:19,922 --> 00:38:21,090
Grandma!

538
00:38:23,050 --> 00:38:25,594
Why are you here? Why did you come?

539
00:38:25,678 --> 00:38:28,014
-Grandma, I'm here. You're okay now.
-Why would you…

540
00:38:28,097 --> 00:38:29,724
What are you going to do?

541
00:38:32,810 --> 00:38:33,728
It's okay now.

542
00:38:33,811 --> 00:38:35,104
-Be careful.
-It's okay.

543
00:38:35,187 --> 00:38:36,897
-It's okay.
-Good heavens.

544
00:38:38,274 --> 00:38:39,275
Oh my goodness.

545
00:39:09,847 --> 00:39:12,767
First off, your favorite things are
boxing and gochujang stew.

546
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:15,936
I've just made it a lot.

547
00:39:16,020 --> 00:39:17,188
Because someone likes it.

548
00:39:46,008 --> 00:39:47,676
OUR STICKY LOVE

549
00:40:34,306 --> 00:40:38,269
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
